  & =41-(a+5)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-109e1a5c-722e-5d5b-b384-b35a60da59b9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-109e1a5c-722e-5d5b-b384-b35a60da59b9" :answer-field/id #uuid "109e1a5c-722e-5d5b-b384-b35a60da59b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-20d0d9be-3816-5756-9034-3199caae3743" :answer-field/choices ["answer-11fa85ec-5f23-5583-a1e2-3b339c957d2a" "answer-dbffa828-6ec7-5c64-9988-48bed410abc3" "answer-b6d26802-0604-5ec9-a6dd-63413f57143a" "answer-20d0d9be-3816-5756-9034-3199caae3743" "answer-6f8b8549-d167-5182-a05e-094b9fd3a421"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11fa85ec-5f23-5583-a1e2-3b339c957d2a" :answer/id #uuid "11fa85ec-5f23-5583-a1e2-3b339c957d2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25-(a+5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dbffa828-6ec7-5c64-9988-48bed410abc3" :answer/id #uuid "dbffa828-6ec7-5c64-9988-48bed410abc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16-(a+5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6d26802-0604-5ec9-a6dd-63413f57143a" :answer/id #uuid "b6d26802-0604-5ec9-a6dd-63413f57143a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25-(a-5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20d0d9be-3816-5756-9034-3199caae3743" :answer/id #uuid "20d0d9be-3816-5756-9034-3199caae3743" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "41-(a+5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f8b8549-d167-5182-a05e-094b9fd3a421" :answer/id #uuid "6f8b8549-d167-5182-a05e-094b9fd3a421" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9-(a-5)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184483 :question/problem "Rewrite $-({y}^{2}-5y+6)$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "We begin by completing the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-5y+6\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}y+6\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $6$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}y+{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+6\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+6\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({y}^{2}-5y+6) & =-({(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186181075 :answer-field/correct "answer-0d6b0b59-5f4d-58eb-aec7-42d212af1618" :answer-field/choices ["answer-91d492cf-1c56-56df-bd04-4aabaf69aec4" "answer-0d6b0b59-5f4d-58eb-aec7-42d212af1618" "answer-6969fc79-b38b-551a-bfdf-07495efdaf43" "answer-fc78b4ea-4ddc-5ed1-8637-95f6e755fa4c" "answer-0710913b-7399-5b9e-a5a9-f4627344dd74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91d492cf-1c56-56df-bd04-4aabaf69aec4" :answer/id #uuid "91d492cf-1c56-56df-bd04-4aabaf69aec4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31-{(y+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d6b0b59-5f4d-58eb-aec7-42d212af1618" :answer/id #uuid "0d6b0b59-5f4d-58eb-aec7-42d212af1618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6969fc79-b38b-551a-bfdf-07495efdaf43" :answer/id #uuid "6969fc79-b38b-551a-bfdf-07495efdaf43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc78b4ea-4ddc-5ed1-8637-95f6e755fa4c" :answer/id #uuid "fc78b4ea-4ddc-5ed1-8637-95f6e755fa4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{49}{4}-{(y+\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0710913b-7399-5b9e-a5a9-f4627344dd74" :answer/id #uuid "0710913b-7399-5b9e-a5a9-f4627344dd74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}-{(y-\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-52455c8c-f427-542e-9cf2-e8b407fdf74f" :question/id #uuid "52455c8c-f427-542e-9cf2-e8b407fdf74f" :question/math-academy-id "q-140407" :question/problem "Rewrite $-{y}^{2}+9y-21$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-1.$ So, we take out a factor of $-1$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-({y}^{2}-9y+21)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-9y+21\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}y+21\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $21$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}y+{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+21\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+21\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{y}^{2}+9y-21 & =-({(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}-{(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-416ac210-0c5c-5b57-b96d-e01801ddf600"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-416ac210-0c5c-5b57-b96d-e01801ddf600" :answer-field/id #uuid "416ac210-0c5c-5b57-b96d-e01801ddf600" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0e2a5228-4d34-5c57-8a6c-a3feb27ed440" :answer-field/choices ["answer-564dbae7-bea0-5bb4-b219-b6f52f82ad54" "answer-0e2a5228-4d34-5c57-8a6c-a3feb27ed440" "answer-2e001848-6114-55d4-898d-e807366debec" "answer-4e4aefa9-79b2-5f3f-9f24-fa82ea18cebc" "answer-4803ab05-0b65-5cb4-92e9-f03eef1b730f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-564dbae7-bea0-5bb4-b219-b6f52f82ad54" :answer/id #uuid "564dbae7-bea0-5bb4-b219-b6f52f82ad54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}+{(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e2a5228-4d34-5c57-8a6c-a3feb27ed440" :answer/id #uuid "0e2a5228-4d34-5c57-8a6c-a3feb27ed440" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}-{(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e001848-6114-55d4-898d-e807366debec" :answer/id #uuid "2e001848-6114-55d4-898d-e807366debec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60-{(y-18)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e4aefa9-79b2-5f3f-9f24-fa82ea18cebc" :answer/id #uuid "4e4aefa9-79b2-5f3f-9f24-fa82ea18cebc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{165}{4}-{(y+\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4803ab05-0b65-5cb4-92e9-f03eef1b730f" :answer/id #uuid "4803ab05-0b65-5cb4-92e9-f03eef1b730f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}-{(y-\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184485 :question/problem "Rewrite $-{x}^{2}-x-3$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-1.$ So, we take out a factor of $-1$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-({x}^{2}+x+3)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x+3\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+3\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $3$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+3\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+3\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{11}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-x-3 & =-({(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{11}{4}) \\\\  & =-{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{11}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{4}-{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186181087 :answer-field/correct "answer-ff8880bf-ffee-5976-8095-806532a97526" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ff8880bf-ffee-5976-8095-806532a97526" "answer-057bf8b9-f4be-51c0-a4d1-d57b29da8233" "answer-61f2ea1d-2d8b-55fa-8520-17155db3eebf" "answer-ddfed3f5-06e5-5e82-b0a9-731fa897dd17" "answer-e4f36cd8-e603-55a8-9ec8-ae98cefb08df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff8880bf-ffee-5976-8095-806532a97526" :answer/id #uuid "ff8880bf-ffee-5976-8095-806532a97526" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{4}-{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-057bf8b9-f4be-51c0-a4d1-d57b29da8233" :answer/id #uuid "057bf8b9-f4be-51c0-a4d1-d57b29da8233" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}-{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61f2ea1d-2d8b-55fa-8520-17155db3eebf" :answer/id #uuid "61f2ea1d-2d8b-55fa-8520-17155db3eebf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{(x+2)}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ddfed3f5-06e5-5e82-b0a9-731fa897dd17" :answer/id #uuid "ddfed3f5-06e5-5e82-b0a9-731fa897dd17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{4}-{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4f36cd8-e603-55a8-9ec8-ae98cefb08df" :answer/id #uuid "e4f36cd8-e603-55a8-9ec8-ae98cefb08df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}-{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6fcb379b-2e62-54ea-ab65-5d0b75f0dbcd" :question/id #uuid "6fcb379b-2e62-54ea-ab65-5d0b75f0dbcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-140530" :question/problem "Rewrite $4{x}^{2}+32x+40$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $4.$ So, we take out a factor of $4$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n4({x}^{2}+8x+10)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+8x+10\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+10\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${4}^{2},$ writing the constant term $10$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2}}_{⏟}-{4}^{2}+10\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x+4)^{2}-{4}^{2}+10\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x+4)^{2}-6\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}^{2}+8x+10) & =4((x+4)^{2}-6) \\\\  & =4{(x+4)}^{2}-4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =4{(x+4)}^{2}-24\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-952c5bf3-9d6e-5030-8f7f-3c940131b3ba"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-952c5bf3-9d6e-5030-8f7f-3c940131b3ba" :answer-field/id #uuid "952c5bf3-9d6e-5030-8f7f-3c940131b3ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-afcdb75c-e813-595d-bae0-066b25d66f82" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9fda3e7d-5801-5dc8-9c05-1ae2500e0fae" "answer-afcdb75c-e813-595d-bae0-066b25d66f82" "answer-d752feaf-59fd-5134-932a-9f884eace22e" "answer-19b4d955-924d-5b66-994e-cd8d4afee070" "answer-f7f4119d-6a4b-5ef7-897f-562be8a71f60"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fda3e7d-5801-5dc8-9c05-1ae2500e0fae" :answer/id #uuid "9fda3e7d-5801-5dc8-9c05-1ae2500e0fae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{(x+4)}^{2}+10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-afcdb75c-e813-595d-bae0-066b25d66f82" :answer/id #uuid "afcdb75c-e813-595d-bae0-066b25d66f82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{(x+4)}^{2}-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d752feaf-59fd-5134-932a-9f884eace22e" :answer/id #uuid "d752feaf-59fd-5134-932a-9f884eace22e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{(x+4)}^{2}-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19b4d955-924d-5b66-994e-cd8d4afee070" :answer/id #uuid "19b4d955-924d-5b66-994e-cd8d4afee070" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{(x+8)}^{2}+40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f7f4119d-6a4b-5ef7-897f-562be8a71f60" :answer/id #uuid "f7f4119d-6a4b-5ef7-897f-562be8a71f60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{(x+8)}^{2}-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a3f44aac-b56c-541f-849d-0822403501d2" :question/id #uuid "a3f44aac-b56c-541f-849d-0822403501d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-52539" :question/problem "Rewrite $7{x}^{2}-21x$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $7.$ So, we take out a factor of $7$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n7({x}^{2}-3x)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-3x\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}:$ \n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last term, we get\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7({x}^{2}-3x) & =7({(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\  & =7{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-7\\cdot \\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =7{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{63}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f7c32e90-669a-52ff-9868-695c63e890c3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f7c32e90-669a-52ff-9868-695c63e890c3" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7c32e90-669a-52ff-9868-695c63e890c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5b9c5aa0-fb14-5496-9591-622a3ce17833" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c7a8f032-2fca-5906-b4f7-ab9bf75bf249" "answer-5b9c5aa0-fb14-5496-9591-622a3ce17833" "answer-0b2204f3-0b9c-5716-8b12-1daaa8e9c98c" "answer-4dcec967-e7ae-5ddf-bf71-07068fba0434" "answer-abd335e9-aa90-5300-ad70-e9bfcbdab375"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7a8f032-2fca-5906-b4f7-ab9bf75bf249" :answer/id #uuid "c7a8f032-2fca-5906-b4f7-ab9bf75bf249" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{49}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b9c5aa0-fb14-5496-9591-622a3ce17833" :answer/id #uuid "5b9c5aa0-fb14-5496-9591-622a3ce17833" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{63}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b2204f3-0b9c-5716-8b12-1daaa8e9c98c" :answer/id #uuid "0b2204f3-0b9c-5716-8b12-1daaa8e9c98c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dcec967-e7ae-5ddf-bf71-07068fba0434" :answer/id #uuid "4dcec967-e7ae-5ddf-bf71-07068fba0434" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(7x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{49}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abd335e9-aa90-5300-ad70-e9bfcbdab375" :answer/id #uuid "abd335e9-aa90-5300-ad70-e9bfcbdab375" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(7x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5eff477c-d77b-5edc-9e57-fb4474642e96" :question/id #uuid "5eff477c-d77b-5edc-9e57-fb4474642e96" :question/math-academy-id "q-218758" :question/problem "Rewrite $10{x}^{2}+2x+\\frac{7}{10}$ by completing the square.\n\n$10{x}^{2}+2x+\\frac{7}{10}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$(x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$)^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $10.$ So, we take out a factor of $10$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n10({x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{10}x+\\frac{7}{100})\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{10}x+\\frac{7}{100}\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}x+\\frac{7}{100}\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $\\frac{7}{100}$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}x+{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+\\frac{7}{100}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+\\frac{7}{100}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{50}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10({x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{10}x+\\frac{7}{100}) & =10({(x+\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{50}) \\\\  & =10{(x+\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+10\\cdot \\frac{3}{50} \\\\  & =10{(x+\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8f40a4d7-d407-5619-8448-b04becc5c8a3" "answer-field-321f92c3-450e-5fba-993b-2e46cd9808aa" "answer-field-78c39176-488f-543b-a2da-3abb77eaa53b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8f40a4d7-d407-5619-8448-b04becc5c8a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f40a4d7-d407-5619-8448-b04becc5c8a3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-15719c4e-b7fb-5170-8bb8-2901fc8bc636" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15719c4e-b7fb-5170-8bb8-2901fc8bc636"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15719c4e-b7fb-5170-8bb8-2901fc8bc636" :answer/id #uuid "15719c4e-b7fb-5170-8bb8-2901fc8bc636" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-321f92c3-450e-5fba-993b-2e46cd9808aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "321f92c3-450e-5fba-993b-2e46cd9808aa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-f0c81066-fa93-57ad-9c31-169594b16f84" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f0c81066-fa93-57ad-9c31-169594b16f84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0c81066-fa93-57ad-9c31-169594b16f84" :answer/id #uuid "f0c81066-fa93-57ad-9c31-169594b16f84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-78c39176-488f-543b-a2da-3abb77eaa53b" :answer-field/id #uuid "78c39176-488f-543b-a2da-3abb77eaa53b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-01ce5e56-780d-5c88-bed9-f6bd700d42ff" :answer-field/choices ["answer-01ce5e56-780d-5c88-bed9-f6bd700d42ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-01ce5e56-780d-5c88-bed9-f6bd700d42ff" :answer/id #uuid "01ce5e56-780d-5c88-bed9-f6bd700d42ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d53c2052-a67a-5988-8f1a-4c9a720c7a75" :question/id #uuid "d53c2052-a67a-5988-8f1a-4c9a720c7a75" :question/math-academy-id "q-52532" :question/problem "Rewrite $-4{x}^{2}+8x$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-4.$ So, we take out a factor of $-4$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-4({x}^{2}-2x)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1x\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${1}^{2}:$ \n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1x+{1}^{2}}_{⏟}-{1}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x-1)}^{2}-{1}^{2}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last term, we get\n\n$$\n{(x-1)}^{2}-1\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4({x}^{2}-2x) & =-4({(x-1)}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =-4{(x-1)}^{2}+(-4)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-4{(x-1)}^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-167b595a-7f5f-59ff-991b-3067a90e82fd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-167b595a-7f5f-59ff-991b-3067a90e82fd" :answer-field/id #uuid "167b595a-7f5f-59ff-991b-3067a90e82fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3b842baa-f6f2-52b1-8460-09b16f0bcd80" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b842baa-f6f2-52b1-8460-09b16f0bcd80" "answer-b561b8c7-15f6-5cfb-b205-0138ec744c67" "answer-307076da-9752-5562-860a-d357b7f3f900" "answer-86e1cc55-8aa1-5b03-a1af-07dc83b72500" "answer-12b3902d-1015-53f0-995d-a66e100771ef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b842baa-f6f2-52b1-8460-09b16f0bcd80" :answer/id #uuid "3b842baa-f6f2-52b1-8460-09b16f0bcd80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{(x-1)}^{2}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b561b8c7-15f6-5cfb-b205-0138ec744c67" :answer/id #uuid "b561b8c7-15f6-5cfb-b205-0138ec744c67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4{(x-1)}^{2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-307076da-9752-5562-860a-d357b7f3f900" :answer/id #uuid "307076da-9752-5562-860a-d357b7f3f900" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{(4x-1)}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86e1cc55-8aa1-5b03-a1af-07dc83b72500" :answer/id #uuid "86e1cc55-8aa1-5b03-a1af-07dc83b72500" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{(x-1)}^{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12b3902d-1015-53f0-995d-a66e100771ef" :answer/id #uuid "12b3902d-1015-53f0-995d-a66e100771ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{(4x-1)}^{2}-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-71daf213-45ae-576f-97ae-9ffbff2f758a" :question/id #uuid "71daf213-45ae-576f-97ae-9ffbff2f758a" :question/math-academy-id "q-52543" :question/problem "Rewrite $-2{x}^{2}-6x$ by completing the square." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-2.$ So, we take out a factor of $-2$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-2({x}^{2}+3x)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+3x\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}:$ \n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last term, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2({x}^{2}+3x) & =-2({(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\  & =-2{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+(-2)\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\  & =-2{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-57fbd290-f3b1-5227-bd0d-a92509c57f4e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-57fbd290-f3b1-5227-bd0d-a92509c57f4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "57fbd290-f3b1-5227-bd0d-a92509c57f4e" :answer-fiel