n-52455c8c-f427-542e-9cf2-e8b407fdf74f" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-416ac210-0c5c-5b57-b96d-e01801ddf600"] [17592186184322 :knowledge-point/questions "question-52455c8c-f427-542e-9cf2-e8b407fdf74f"] [17592186184485 :question/problem "Rewrite $-{x}^{2}-x-3$ by completing the square."] [17592186184485 :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-1.$ So, we take out a factor of $-1$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-({x}^{2}+x+3)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x+3\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+3\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $3$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+3\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+3\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{11}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}-x-3 & =-({(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{11}{4}) \\\\  & =-{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{11}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{4}-{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186184485 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-ff8880bf-ffee-5976-8095-806532a97526" :answer/id #uuid "ff8880bf-ffee-5976-8095-806532a97526"] ["answer-ff8880bf-ffee-5976-8095-806532a97526" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ff8880bf-ffee-5976-8095-806532a97526" :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{4}-{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}"] ["answer-057bf8b9-f4be-51c0-a4d1-d57b29da8233" :answer/id #uuid "057bf8b9-f4be-51c0-a4d1-d57b29da8233"] ["answer-057bf8b9-f4be-51c0-a4d1-d57b29da8233" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-057bf8b9-f4be-51c0-a4d1-d57b29da8233" :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}-{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}"] ["answer-61f2ea1d-2d8b-55fa-8520-17155db3eebf" :answer/id #uuid "61f2ea1d-2d8b-55fa-8520-17155db3eebf"] ["answer-61f2ea1d-2d8b-55fa-8520-17155db3eebf" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-61f2ea1d-2d8b-55fa-8520-17155db3eebf" :answer/value "1-{(x+2)}^{2}"] ["answer-ddfed3f5-06e5-5e82-b0a9-731fa897dd17" :answer/id #uuid "ddfed3f5-06e5-5e82-b0a9-731fa897dd17"] ["answer-ddfed3f5-06e5-5e82-b0a9-731fa897dd17" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ddfed3f5-06e5-5e82-b0a9-731fa897dd17" :answer/value "\\frac{10}{4}-{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}"] ["answer-e4f36cd8-e603-55a8-9ec8-ae98cefb08df" :answer/id #uuid "e4f36cd8-e603-55a8-9ec8-ae98cefb08df"] ["answer-e4f36cd8-e603-55a8-9ec8-ae98cefb08df" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e4f36cd8-e603-55a8-9ec8-ae98cefb08df" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}-{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}"] [17592186181087 :answer-field/correct "answer-ff8880bf-ffee-5976-8095-806532a97526"] [17592186181087 :answer-field/choices "answer-ff8880bf-ffee-5976-8095-806532a97526"] [17592186181087 :answer-field/choices "answer-057bf8b9-f4be-51c0-a4d1-d57b29da8233"] [17592186181087 :answer-field/choices "answer-61f2ea1d-2d8b-55fa-8520-17155db3eebf"] [17592186181087 :answer-field/choices "answer-ddfed3f5-06e5-5e82-b0a9-731fa897dd17"] [17592186181087 :answer-field/choices "answer-e4f36cd8-e603-55a8-9ec8-ae98cefb08df"] ["question-6fcb379b-2e62-54ea-ab65-5d0b75f0dbcd" :question/id #uuid "6fcb379b-2e62-54ea-ab65-5d0b75f0dbcd"] ["question-6fcb379b-2e62-54ea-ab65-5d0b75f0dbcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-140530"] ["question-6fcb379b-2e62-54ea-ab65-5d0b75f0dbcd" :question/problem "Rewrite $4{x}^{2}+32x+40$ by completing the square."] ["question-6fcb379b-2e62-54ea-ab65-5d0b75f0dbcd" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $4.$ So, we take out a factor of $4$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n4({x}^{2}+8x+10)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+8x+10\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+10\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${4}^{2},$ writing the constant term $10$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2}}_{⏟}-{4}^{2}+10\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n(x+4)^{2}-{4}^{2}+10\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n(x+4)^{2}-6\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}^{2}+8x+10) & =4((x+4)^{2}-6) \\\\  & =4{(x+4)}^{2}-4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =4{(x+4)}^{2}-24\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-6fcb379b-2e62-54ea-ab65-5d0b75f0dbcd" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-952c5bf3-9d6e-5030-8f7f-3c940131b3ba" :answer-field/id #uuid "952c5bf3-9d6e-5030-8f7f-3c940131b3ba"] ["answer-9fda3e7d-5801-5dc8-9c05-1ae2500e0fae" :answer/id #uuid "9fda3e7d-5801-5dc8-9c05-1ae2500e0fae"] ["answer-9fda3e7d-5801-5dc8-9c05-1ae2500e0fae" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9fda3e7d-5801-5dc8-9c05-1ae2500e0fae" :answer/value "4{(x+4)}^{2}+10"] ["answer-afcdb75c-e813-595d-bae0-066b25d66f82" :answer/id #uuid "afcdb75c-e813-595d-bae0-066b25d66f82"] ["answer-afcdb75c-e813-595d-bae0-066b25d66f82" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-afcdb75c-e813-595d-bae0-066b25d66f82" :answer/value "4{(x+4)}^{2}-24"] ["answer-d752feaf-59fd-5134-932a-9f884eace22e" :answer/id #uuid "d752feaf-59fd-5134-932a-9f884eace22e"] ["answer-d752feaf-59fd-5134-932a-9f884eace22e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d752feaf-59fd-5134-932a-9f884eace22e" :answer/value "4{(x+4)}^{2}-6"] ["answer-19b4d955-924d-5b66-994e-cd8d4afee070" :answer/id #uuid "19b4d955-924d-5b66-994e-cd8d4afee070"] ["answer-19b4d955-924d-5b66-994e-cd8d4afee070" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-19b4d955-924d-5b66-994e-cd8d4afee070" :answer/value "4{(x+8)}^{2}+40"] ["answer-f7f4119d-6a4b-5ef7-897f-562be8a71f60" :answer/id #uuid "f7f4119d-6a4b-5ef7-897f-562be8a71f60"] 