e out a factor of $10$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n10({x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{10}x+\\frac{7}{100})\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{10}x+\\frac{7}{100}\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}x+\\frac{7}{100}\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $\\frac{7}{100}$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}x+{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}}_{⏟}-\\,{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+\\frac{7}{100}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+\\frac{7}{100}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{50}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10({x}^{2}+\\frac{2}{10}x+\\frac{7}{100}) & =10({(x+\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{50}) \\\\  & =10{(x+\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+10\\cdot \\frac{3}{50} \\\\  & =10{(x+\\frac{1}{10})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-5eff477c-d77b-5edc-9e57-fb4474642e96" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-8f40a4d7-d407-5619-8448-b04becc5c8a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f40a4d7-d407-5619-8448-b04becc5c8a3"] ["answer-15719c4e-b7fb-5170-8bb8-2901fc8bc636" :answer/id #uuid "15719c4e-b7fb-5170-8bb8-2901fc8bc636"] ["answer-15719c4e-b7fb-5170-8bb8-2901fc8bc636" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-15719c4e-b7fb-5170-8bb8-2901fc8bc636" :answer/value "10"] ["answer-field-8f40a4d7-d407-5619-8448-b04becc5c8a3" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-8f40a4d7-d407-5619-8448-b04becc5c8a3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-8f40a4d7-d407-5619-8448-b04becc5c8a3" :answer-field/correct "answer-15719c4e-b7fb-5170-8bb8-2901fc8bc636"] ["answer-field-8f40a4d7-d407-5619-8448-b04becc5c8a3" :answer-field/choices "answer-15719