ion-71daf213-45ae-576f-97ae-9ffbff2f758a" :question/id #uuid "71daf213-45ae-576f-97ae-9ffbff2f758a"] ["question-71daf213-45ae-576f-97ae-9ffbff2f758a" :question/math-academy-id "q-52543"] ["question-71daf213-45ae-576f-97ae-9ffbff2f758a" :question/problem "Rewrite $-2{x}^{2}-6x$ by completing the square."] ["question-71daf213-45ae-576f-97ae-9ffbff2f758a" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the leading coefficient is $-2.$ So, we take out a factor of $-2$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n-2({x}^{2}+3x)\n$$\n\nLet's now complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+3x\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x\n$$\n\nThen, we *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}:$ \n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the last term, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2({x}^{2}+3x) & =-2({(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\  & =-2{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+(-2)\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\  & =-2{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-71daf213-45ae-576f-97ae-9ffbff2f758a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-57fbd290-f3b1-5227-bd0d-a92509c57f4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "57fbd290-f3b1-5227-bd0d-a92509c57f4e"] ["answer-44526162-1855-508d-ad71-02db10f1e1b8" :answer/id #uuid "44526162-1855-508d-ad71-02db10f1e1b8"] ["answer-44526162-1855-508d-ad71-02db10f1e1b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-44526162-1855-508d-ad71-02db10f1e1b8" :answer/value "-2{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}+\\frac{9}{2}"] ["answer-4e6d2b6a-5266-5c53-ac87-e02a1827047e" :answer/id #uuid "4e6d2b6a-5266-5c53-ac87-e02a1827047e"] ["answ